   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT relating to authorizing the district superintendent of the\nEastport-South Manor central school district to adjust the improper\napportionment of the school tax levy which occurred in the 2019-2020 tax year\nover the next two tax years (2020-2021 and 2021-2022) and validating certain\nacts by the Eastport-South Manor central school district in connection with\nadjustment of the improper apportionment of the school tax levy in 2019-2020",
    "basePrintNo": "S5750",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5750-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5750\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act relating to authorizing the district superintendent of the East-\nport-South Manor central school district to adjust the improper appor-\ntionment of the school tax levy which occurred in the 2019-2020 tax year\nover the next two tax years (2020-2021 and 2021-2022) and validating\ncertain acts by the Eastport-South Manor central school district in\nconnection with adjustment of the improper apportionment of the school\ntax levy in 2019-2020\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the district superintendent of the Eastport-South Manor\nCentral School District to adjust certain improper apportionments of\nschool tax levy.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 Authorizes the district superintendent of the Eastport-South\nManor Central School District (CSD) to adjust certain improper appor-\ntionments of school tax levy that was based upon a mathematical error.\n\nSection 2. Legalizes, validates, ratifies and confirms the manner in\nwhich the Eastport-South Manor CSD superintendent adjusted the improper\napportionments of the school tax levy that was based upon a mathematical\nerror notwithstanding the unintentional failure to comply with the\nprovisions of subdivision 3 of section 1314 of the real property law or\nany other law or any other statutory authority, rule or regulation in\nrelation to any omission, error, effect, irregularity or illegality in\nsuch proceeding had taken.\n\nSection 3 sets an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Eastport-South Manor CSD is comprised of taxpayers from the town of\nSouthampton and the town of Brookhaven (mostly Brookhaven). The voters\napprove the school district budget, which is funded in part by the State\nand the total amount that needs to be collected is divided between the\ntwo taxing jurisdictions.\n\nDue to a mathematical error, the 2019-20 equalization rate was miscalcu-\nlated and resulted with the Southampton town residents paying less taxes\nthan were owed, while the Brookhaven town residents paid more. To\naccount for this adjustment and to lessen the fiscal impact, the East-\nport-South Manor CSD superintendent adjusted the improper apportionment\nby including half of the amount that Southampton underpaid in 2020 in\ntheir 2021 tax bill, with the remainder due in their 2022 tax bill.\nWhile well intentioned, this remedy is inconsistent with the provisions\nof section 1314(3) of the real property tax law which requires a redress\nto occur in the subsequent assessment roll. This legislation is neces-\nsary to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm the manner in which the\nEastport-South Manor CSD superintendent adjusted the improper apportion-\nments of the school tax levy that was based upon a mathematical error\nnotwithstanding the unintentional failure to comply with the provisions\nof section 1314(3) of the real property law or any other law or any\nother statutory authority, rule or regulation in relation to any omis-\nsion, error, defect irregularity or illegality in such proceeding had\nand taken.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
